BEGIN:VEVENT
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://map-india.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/MAP-Website-1.jpg
CATEGORIES:Guided Walk,MAP,CBD
DTSTAMP:20261006T120213Z
DESCRIPTION:Join Aayati Sengupta\, Curator of Grip\, Hold\, Pin\, for a walkthrough of the exhibition. Through a close reading of the works on view\, the walkthrough will explore wrestling as more than a sport—as a site where discipline\, kinship\, identity and everyday life converge. Drawing on photography\, archival material and moving image\, Grip\, Hold\, Pin traces the histories and lived experiences that shape wrestling cultures across India\, inviting audiences to consider the relationships between body\, labour\, tradition and representation.
DTEND:20261011T063000Z
DTSTART:20261011T053000Z
SUMMARY:Grip\, Hold\, Pin - Curator walkthrough
UID:1415@map-india.org
URL:https://map-india.org/map-events/grip-hold-pin-curator-walkthrough/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://map-india.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/MAP-Website-9.jpg
CATEGORIES:Talks,MAP,CBD
DTSTAMP:20261008T074821Z
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a conversation around writer and publisher Sudhanva Deshpande’s new book\, Imposter: The Playful Subversions of Orijit Sen. \n\nSpanning four decades of Orijit Sen’s practice\, the book traces the artist’s journey through comics\, graphic storytelling\, political satire\, design and visual culture. From River of Stories\, India’s first graphic novel\, to the many forms his work has taken since\, Sen has continually played with the possibilities of the image and the page. Moderated by Lakshmi Karunakaran\, the conversation reflects Orijit’s practice\, influences and experiments\, and the ideas behind the book. 
DTEND:20261017T130000Z
DTSTART:20261017T113000Z
SUMMARY:Book Launch - Imposter: The Playful Subversions of Orijit Sen
UID:1419@map-india.org
URL:https://map-india.org/map-events/book-launch-imposter-the-playful-subversions-of-orijit-sen/
END:VEVENT
